WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.740
In 2023, Equatorial Guinea
produced about 6,800 US dollars

2
00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:07.690
of output per person.

3
00:00:07.690 --> 00:00:11.100
Sri Lanka produced about 3,800.

4
00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:16.070
So Equatorial Guinea made about
1.8 times as much per person.

5
00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:20.090
In Niger, 74 per cent
of jobs are in farming.

6
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.900
In the UK, under 1 per cent.

7
00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:26.780
So does more output per person
mean people live better?

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:28.840
And how can we measure the gap?

9
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.880
In this mission, you'll
work out GDP per head

10
00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:34.690
and weigh up its strengths and weaknesses.

11
00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:38.770
Then you'll see how jobs shift
between sectors as countries develop,

12
00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:41.780
and why some get stuck
in a vicious circle.

13
00:00:41.780 --> 00:00:45.150
Your mission: find out what
really makes living standards

14
00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:47.350
higher in one country than another,

15
00:00:47.350 --> 00:00:48.670
and how to measure them.
